{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy","id":1538938,"title":"Ideas for an Obrimos Death Legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-20T03:47:45-07:00","id":1538938,"title":"Ideas for an Obrimos Death Legacy","content":"This is a just-for-fun thought exercise, but I've always found it very hard to come up with a good Death-Primary Legacy that actually fits the Obrimos themes and isn't just arbitrarily tacking on the Path. A few Legacies in general don't really resonate enough with their Parent Path and could work just as well (if not outright better) if they originated with another Path entirely (looking at you, Reality Makers and Whipping Boys). The problem is further compounded in this case because, firstly, Death is so strongly thematically associated with the Moros, making it hard to come up with a non-Moros Death Legacy that actually feels thematically proprietary to its Parent Path without going for soul stuff, which has kind of been done to death (lol?). Secondly, compared to other Inferior Arcana, Death seems the most thematically distant from the Path that has it as Inferior. Even write-ups in books like the 2e Core, Signs of Sorcery, and Summoners don't give much inspiration for a workaround, and in fact seem to reinforce this thematic divide between the Obrimos and Death.<br /> <br /> I've come up with a few ideas myself, but never ones that really satisfied me. One was a Legacy focused on the destructive aspects of Death and Forces, but this again didn't really feel like it resonated the most or even enough with the Obrimos and was basically a lame Masters of Destruction rehash. Another more promising concept involved the idea of &quot;ghosts of dead stars&quot; in link with the Black Huriyah from Mummy 1e's Book of the Deceived, with this Legacy seeking the black angels as the only remnants of cosmic embodiments of power, or maybe to appease them in the hopes of rebirthing dead stars or something. This idea fell flat due to it better working with Spirit rather than Death, especially since the Black Huriyah seem a lot like void spirits, albeit Duat-adjacent. I also couldn't think of a less nebulous goal/Theory for the Legacy. I've also seen some other fan-made Obrimos Death Legacies, but never felt any avoided the problems I outlined above enough. However, I'd be very interested in hearing other ideas from the good folks on the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T16:24:56-07:00","id":1538955,"title":"","content":"Perhaps something concerned with being a beacon of inspiration in the Underworld? Empowering ghosts with a sense of grandeur and higher purpose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T09:12:37-07:00","id":1538970,"title":"","content":"What about a Legacy of ink painters ? In the Aether, Death is less expressive because things are constantly changing, destruction leading to creation. So why wouldn't emptiness itself change, becoming a source of potential ? Wielding shadows as their ink, they shape them into avenues of self expression. Imbuing them with the power of Prime, they can be given substance, forming and greater purpose (such as a capstone combining elements of <i>Eidolon</i> and <i>Create Ghost</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T13:13:36-07:00","id":1538987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1538955#post1538955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps something concerned with being a beacon of inspiration in the Underworld? Empowering ghosts with a sense of grandeur and higher purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both ideas fit just as well with the Moros unfortunately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1538970#post1538970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a Legacy of ink painters ? In the Aether, Death is less expressive because things are constantly changing, destruction leading to creation. So why wouldn't emptiness itself change, becoming a source of potential ? Wielding shadows as their ink, they shape them into avenues of self expression. Imbuing them with the power of Prime, they can be given substance, forming and greater purpose (such as a capstone combining elements of <i>Eidolon</i> and <i>Create Ghost</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting concept. The imagery calls to mind the Silverquill mages from Magic: The Gathering, while the magical theory reminds me of the Tamers of the Cave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T13:37:55-07:00","id":1538991,"title":"","content":"What comes to mind for me is admittedly not as broadly useful, but an Abyssal Legacy taking &quot;inspiration&quot; from the Deluge Obrimos Nasnasi align themselves with seems apropos.<br /> <br /> The tricky thing with Death and the Obrimos, to not put too fine a point on it, is that thematically the Path of the Mighty relates to stuff that generally signifies sustained positive existence \u2014 light, fire, sound, presence, the Essence of the fivefold soul \u2014 and Death is chiefly used for messing with the end product of a given state of existence. There's no small number of Life-based Obrimos Legacies for the same reason the Path resonates with enduring and &quot;perfected&quot; materials like gold and steel, but even without the Death Arcanum being tightly linked to the Moros it's hard to find a Path-related basis for the category of wizard that has a radiant Nimbus and a hefty symbolic overlap with secular and sectarian power to focus on the bywords for the taboo that are darkness and the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T14:24:15-07:00","id":1538993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1538987#post1538987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both ideas fit just as well with the Moros unfortunately.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, how exactly? The themes of Moros strike me as a lot more &quot;let go&quot; than &quot;ghosts are awesome&quot;. <br /> <br /> On the other, does it matter? I think &quot;no thematic overlap with the Path that has it as a Ruling Arcanum&quot; would exclude a lot of existing Legacies. What is the higher priority here, to have something totally proscriptive, or something that gives an Obrimos inroads to this that are both consistent with and kind of subversive to the themes of their Path?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T12:01:12-07:00","id":1539108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1538993#post1538993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, how exactly? The themes of Moros strike me as a lot more &quot;let go&quot; than &quot;ghosts are awesome&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really get &quot;ghosts are awesome&quot; from your first post but saw it more as empowering ghosts is also a path to letting go, which as you said is more of a Moros theme, and hence my feeling that the idea isn't sufficiently resonant with the Obrimos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1538993#post1538993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other, does it matter? I think &quot;no thematic overlap with the Path that has it as a Ruling Arcanum&quot; would exclude a lot of existing Legacies. What is the higher priority here, to have something totally proscriptive, or something that gives an Obrimos inroads to this that are both consistent with and kind of subversive to the themes of their Path?</div> </div> </div> </div>The priority's definitely the latter, but in a way that's sufficiently thematic for the Obrimos without borrowing too much from the Moros.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1538991#post1538991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What comes to mind for me is admittedly not as broadly useful, but an Abyssal Legacy taking &quot;inspiration&quot; from the Deluge Obrimos Nasnasi align themselves with seems apropos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting idea. The eschatological angle's a good source of inspiration, but not very easy to execute satisfactorily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1538991#post1538991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tricky thing with Death and the Obrimos, to not put too fine a point on it, is that thematically the Path of the Mighty relates to stuff that generally signifies sustained positive existence \u2014 light, fire, sound, presence, the Essence of the fivefold soul \u2014 and Death is chiefly used for messing with the end product of a given state of existence. There's no small number of Life-based Obrimos Legacies for the same reason the Path resonates with enduring and &quot;perfected&quot; materials like gold and steel, but even without the Death Arcanum being tightly linked to the Moros it's hard to find a Path-related basis for the category of wizard that has a radiant Nimbus and a hefty symbolic overlap with secular and sectarian power to focus on the bywords for the taboo that are darkness and the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a tough nut to crack...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T17:40:57-07:00","id":1539121,"title":"","content":"Going off what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> said, I was wondering about a legacy based upon doing something with ghost mages? Like, Mummy 2e has the concept of a cult including ghosts. There's a mention in one of the books of Atlantis having had a place where the ghosts of dead mages would hang out so that living mages could benefit from their knowledge. So why would the Pentacle not do the same? (I mean, I suspect there <i>are</i> actually good reasons not to, but a legacy might have different ideas).<br /> <br /> Thinking along those lines I could see an Arrow/Obrimos legacy based on allowing Talons to keep upholding their oaths even once they're ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T03:54:42-07:00","id":1539137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539108#post1539108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't really get &quot;ghosts are awesome&quot; from your first post but saw it more as empowering ghosts is <b>a path to letting go</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's a thing you've brought to it.<br /> <br /> Be an Obrimos. Give ghosts anchors of being awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T05:28:36-07:00","id":1539140,"title":"","content":"How about a legacy based on a deity?<br /> <br /> This deity was an Obrimos mage, when they died he left a very aware ghost.<br /> <br /> During millenia, this ghost has been guiding the members of the Legacy with magic knowledge and instructions to resurrect him.<br /> This resurrection, temporary, allows this deity to &quot;build&quot; a step of the Silver Ladder before dying again.<br /> <br /> The idea for the Legacy is to keep on with the cycle so eventually the deity will be able to restore the ladder fully.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6914-javimanzano","name":"JaviManzano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T06:46:20-07:00","id":1539141,"title":"","content":"How about something the Obrimos themes of divinity, tying it to deathly gods like Hel. But at the same time opposing defying the Moros idea of seeing death as a transition by having a strong theme of not letting death change you. Accept Death is a part of you, but do not accept Death, master it and bend it to your will.<br /> <br /> Initiation rites would amount to killing yourself then powering through death to go on living. The end result is they have bodies that are part dead (less dead is more prestigious). Often being a mixture of living flesh, dead organic matter, Ectoplasm and Eidolon.<br /> <br /> Having &quot;Mastered Death&quot; they have powers like commanding ghosts, opening Avernun gates, and their capstone is reflexively casting Deny the Reaper when killed making them not quite, but almost unkillable. Maybe it costs a willpower point every time so you can put them down for good if you keep doing it.<br /> <br /> Members have a tendency to set themselves up like kings, giving ghosts a chance to feel more alive in exchange for feilty. Powerful ones rule whole kingdoms in the Underworld. The Legacy claims its end goal is to restore the Underworld under the reign of benevolent gods dispensing eternal rewards or punishment as appropriate. Others claim they just want to rule.<br /> <br /> Orders, maybe Silver Ladder. Possibly with (rumours that tyrants ruling underworld kingdoms and building monuments to their glory are Seers are false. They're Hubristic members of the Ladder)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T14:09:08-07:00","id":1539245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539137#post1539137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be an Obrimos. Give ghosts anchors of being awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm a bit too hung-up on the perception of ghosts as &quot;too Moros&quot; and &quot;too not-Obrimos&quot; but I can see your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539121#post1539121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going off what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> said, I was wondering about a legacy based upon doing something with ghost mages? Like, Mummy 2e has the concept of a cult including ghosts. There's a mention in one of the books of Atlantis having had a place where the ghosts of dead mages would hang out so that living mages could benefit from their knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the Cenacle of Sighs, mentioned in Grimoire of Grimoires. Good idea for a Mysterium Legacy, but I don't feel it fits the Obrimos angle that much. Generally speaking, though, Mummy's a great source of inspiration for Legacies and other Mage stuff in general. You can easily come up with good Legacies based on the Decrees, the Guilds, or the Deceived Temakh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thinking along those lines I could see an Arrow/Obrimos legacy based on allowing Talons to keep upholding their oaths even once they're ghosts. </div> </div> </div>I had a similar idea of Obrimos Arrows who mastered Death to become deathless soldiers but couldn't sufficiently flesh it out or justify the use of Death over Life. Your idea at least solves the latter issue but as is evident I'm personally pretty iffy on trying to associate the Obrimos with ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JaviManzano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539140#post1539140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a legacy based on a deity?<br /> <br /> This deity was an Obrimos mage, when they died he left a very aware ghost.<br /> <br /> During millenia, this ghost has been guiding the members of the Legacy with magic knowledge and instructions to resurrect him.<br /> This resurrection, temporary, allows this deity to &quot;build&quot; a step of the Silver Ladder before dying again.<br /> <br /> The idea for the Legacy is to keep on with the cycle so eventually the deity will be able to restore the ladder fully.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Very</i> interesting idea. Lots of good plot hooks like how true the Legacy's premise is and the conflict that creates if it <i>is</i> true. Using Death for such a specific purpose to achieve something grandiose and eternal also neatly sidesteps using Moros themes too much while being recognisably Obrimos.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539141#post1539141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about something the Obrimos themes of divinity, tying it to deathly gods like Hel. But at the same time opposing defying the Moros idea of seeing death as a transition by having a strong theme of not letting death change you. Accept Death is a part of you, but do not accept Death, master it and bend it to your will.<br /> <br /> Initiation rites would amount to killing yourself then powering through death to go on living. The end result is they have bodies that are part dead (less dead is more prestigious). Often being a mixture of living flesh, dead organic matter, Ectoplasm and Eidolon.<br /> <br /> Having &quot;Mastered Death&quot; they have powers like commanding ghosts, opening Avernun gates, and their capstone is reflexively casting Deny the Reaper when killed making them not quite, but almost unkillable. Maybe it costs a willpower point every time so you can put them down for good if you keep doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis has similarity with the second concept Michael mentioned above, but I feel the half-dead body thing is a bit too spiritually icky for even Obrimos who truck with Death.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Legacy claims its end goal is to restore the Underworld under the reign of benevolent gods dispensing eternal rewards or punishment as appropriate. </div> </div> </div>Trying to restore the Underworld is definitely a great idea for an Aspiration/Obsession, though I would personally make this a Moros Legacy's focus rather than an Obrimos one's, but the &quot;new death gods&quot; angle works for the latter too, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Going to re-read Geist 2e and Book of the Dead for more inspiration but loving the brainstorming in the thread so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","user":"Obsidian Pharaoh","date":". 09-08-2024, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T15:04:48-07:00","id":1539254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539245#post1539245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm a bit too hung-up on the perception of ghosts as &quot;too Moros&quot; and &quot;too not-Obrimos&quot; but I can see your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be blunt, I think you are.<br /> <br /> To my mind, the Moros arcana symbolism is deeply anti-ghost. Like, yeah, their Path gives them power over them, but it's all about change and moving on, the thing that definitionally ghosts don't do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T01:40:39-07:00","id":1539298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539245#post1539245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm a bit too hung-up on the perception of ghosts as &quot;too Moros&quot; and &quot;too not-Obrimos&quot; but I can see your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an area where I think it's important to try and isolate what is innate to an Arcanum, rather than a function of the Path to which it is Ruling.<br /> <br /> To me, that's always been the most obvious with Space and its whole thesis of &quot;things are as close as they feel&quot;. That's innate to how Space spells work, and Signs of Sorcery shows how every Path utilizes that symbolism, even if Mastigos is the only one to base the whole thesis statement in it.<br /> <br /> After all, any Obrimos can actually become a Master of Death even while it's their Inferior Arcanum. They need tutelage from a Moros because the symbols of Death are least intuitive to them, but the Moros is still teaching the Arcanum itself, and not their Path. That Master will still wield the Obrimos symbols of Death.<br /> <br /> And the Obrimos symbols of Death are much like their symbols of Forces and Prime, conceiving of reality in terms of function and hierarchy in some kind of grand design.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are a big part of the Death Arcanum because they're a big thing resulting from death and revolving around death and caught in the tangle of the world's death flavoured metaphysics. Moros see all that in terms of transition and finality and the friction against those things, but that's not the only way of seeing ghosts and their big part of the Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T01:56:25-07:00","id":1539300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539254#post1539254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my mind, the Moros arcana symbolism is deeply anti-ghost. Like, yeah, their Path gives them power over them, but it's all about change and moving on, the thing that definitionally ghosts don't do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go that far. I think there's an empathy for ghosts, even if there's a concern for ghosts resolving their anchors and moving on. In fairness, that's a concern ghosts often have as well.<br /> <br /> I think Moros perspective on ghosts could well just be not that they are people who died but can't move on but people created by somebody else's death made up of what they were attached to in life, and often with a driving existential goal of seeing those anchors to their conclusion.<br /> <br /> Sometimes that comes from a place of thinking the ghost goes somewhere, sometimes it's just about letting the last thing they do in an unpleasant existence be fulfilling and purposeful so they slip peacefully into non-existence.<br /> <br /> Moros can be concerned with the larger mystery of why people can be so attached to life in the face of death that it can create entire people to continue embodying those attachments, but that need not always take precedent over engaging with those people.<br /> <br /> I'd say Obrimos may or may not be concerned with resolution of anchors (the prior suggestion of giving them more was honestly a bit hasty), but either way are probably going to see the metaphysics behind why ghosts exist as having purpose and value in its own right, rather than just a consequence of human weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T14:33:48-07:00","id":1539497,"title":"","content":"You could do a Guardians of the Veil type mage who was concerned with putting to rest harmful magic using Prime and Death. I figure you could take the philosophy that magic itself is alive, and you can have it pass on, or even send it down an Avernian gate.<br /> Your first attainment could be something like universal counterspell but using dots in both prime and death to make it super effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T14:50:24-07:00","id":1539499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hydrophiliak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1539497#post1539497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do a Guardians of the Veil type mage who was concerned with putting to rest harmful magic using Prime and Death. I figure you could take the philosophy that magic itself is alive, and you can have it pass on, or even send it down an Avernian gate.<br /> Your first attainment could be something like universal counterspell but using dots in both prime and death to make it super effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on that idea, they could also have a version of <i>Decay</i> that corrodes spells. Make them sanctioned hunters of Banishers and Rapt, protecting mages and Sleepers from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T18:55:56-07:00","id":1539672,"title":"","content":"You could have a Death-focused Obrimos Legacy that centers around the void or negative existence. They would essentially be mystics focusing on the unmanifest form of Deity. Arguably Prime would be a better fit, but just in terms of effects, Death lets you do more shadow stuff. You could also work in primordial chaos mythemes and the like, in which the universe is a vast darkness which is shaped by a divine will. There would be some overlap with the Eyes of Ain Soph, but there would probably be less of a focus on understanding the underpinnings of magic. <br /> <br /> Actually having the Death-themed Legacy deal with ghosts is a bit tricky, but it could still probably work. You could have a necromancer Legacy focused upon compelling information from the dead. Thematically, they would be like grimoire necromancers from the medieval era. Get an intermediary spirit to fetch ghosts from you, use divine authority to compel information from them, and then send them back to the grave. There is a tradition of the ghosts of magicians being summoned by living magicians in order to acquire their knowledge that you could mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T01:18:49-07:00","id":1539980,"title":"","content":"I have two Obrimos Death legacies in mind, although I've never written anything up about them;<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Death + Prime is about the death of magic. Idk if this would be a banisher legacy where they are going around destroying magic, or if it would be a Mysterium legacy that is about pancryptia</li> <li>Death + Forces which would just be about entropy</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T18:07:04-07:00","id":1540023,"title":"","content":"You could do a Death + Forces legacy focusing on the shadows aspect of death, it's a bit undersung in the arcana. Maybe attainments like telekinesis, but you have to have your shadow grasp the object you're influencing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T17:08:54-07:00","id":1541367,"title":"","content":"Maybe something involving black holes? Using gravity and shadows as a theme, or the death of information?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T15:25:09-07:00","id":1541664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1538938-ideas-for-an-obrimos-death-legacy?p=1541367#post1541367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe something involving black holes? Using gravity and shadows as a theme, or the death of information?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aesthetically, I like the idea of using black holes and shadow imagery. The Legacy having a less visceral, physical connection with death would be understandable, given how that is more the domain of the Moros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T16:56:04-07:00","id":1541712,"title":"","content":"Another idea would be to use Death and Forces to harness the power of absolute zero, wielding and shaping ice.<br /> <br /> You could also use the same Arcana combination to make a ninja Legacy. Going invisible, becoming utterly silent, transforming into a shadow to move around unimpeded, creating ninja tools out of shadow or weapons that can immobilize a target, etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user